1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:04,350
The One Ring spent about two thousand four
hundred and sixty years at the bottom

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,623
of a river.

3
00:00:05,983 --> 00:00:08,993
Here's its whole life,
in a track of its own.

4
00:00:09,043 --> 00:00:12,553
Forged around the year sixteen
hundred of the Second Age.

5
00:00:12,603 --> 00:00:17,447
Cut from Sauron's hand. Lost in the
Anduin in the Third Age's second year.

6
00:00:17,797 --> 00:00:21,947
Déagol finds it. Then nearly
five hundred years with Gollum,

7
00:00:21,997 --> 00:00:25,227
until Bilbo picks it up.
Seventy-eight years after that,

8
00:00:25,277 --> 00:00:26,764
it's destroyed.

9
00:00:27,114 --> 00:00:30,444
Nearly five thousand
years, across two Ages.

10
00:00:30,494 --> 00:00:34,413
Keeping a canon of your own?
OpenChronology is free.
